{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9LQFeCBSZXTR8LKRyMdYX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Codex CLI version pin — PLAN-081 Phase 6 / R1 C5 BLOCKING per TDE MF-6\n2\t#\n3\t# Format: semver range. release.yml step 15 + scripts/local/pair-rail-gate.sh\n4\t# pre-flight assert that `codex --version` resolves to a version in this range.\n5\t# Pin update ceremony: requires Phase 4-bis re-run + GPG sign + ADR amendment\n6\t# IF catch_rate shifts >5pp on the locked corpus.\n7\t#\n8\t# Initial range chosen to cover the Phase 0A SPIKE-VERDICT.md baseline.\n9\t#\n10\t# v1.16.0 update (Phase 6-bis 2026-05-11 S101-cont): widened upper bound\n11\t# to <0.131.0 so Owner's actual binary at codex-cli 0.130.0 is in-range.\n12\t# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol, this widening does NOT trigger Phase\n13\t# 4-bis re-run because no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken\n14\t# yet (initial corpus run is itself part of v1.16.0 GA scope). If post-GA\n15\t# the promotion-gate run shows catch_rate shift >5pp on 0.130.x vs\n16\t# 0.128.x baseline, ADR-111 amendment + corpus re-run triggers.\n17\t#\n18\t# PLAN-142 update (S246 2026-06-19): widened upper bound to <0.140.0 so the\n19\t# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.139.0 is in-range — the migration that restored\n20\t# the pair-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin\n21\t# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain\n22\t# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per\n23\t# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check\n24\t# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.\n25\t#\n26\t# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to\n27\t# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the\n28\t# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are\n29\t# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED\n30\t# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an\n31\t# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a\n32\t# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release\n33\t# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).\n34\t# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md\n35\t# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose\n36\t# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`\n37\t# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|\n38\t# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;\n39\t# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869\n40\t# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner\n41\t# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).\n42\t#\n43\t# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to\n44\t# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump\n45\t# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already\n46\t# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n47\t# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release\n48\t# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182\n49\t# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json, re-pinned in this same pack:\n50\t# payload sha256 19c4f144... for 0.147.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity\n51\t# recorded from the platform artifact) remains the real supply-chain gate;\n52\t# this semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n53\t# Locked-corpus catch_rate check (ADR-111 §2): Owner elects run-vs-defer at\n54\t# pack signing, recorded in the SENT-S318 sentinel Scope.\n55\t\n56\t# PLAN-189 update (S352 2026-09-15): widened upper bound to <0.155.0 so the\n57\t# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.154.0 is in-range. The rail was pinned at\n58\t# 0.147.0 while the global CLI had moved SEVEN releases ahead, so every rail\n59\t# round ran on a revisor older than the one the Owner uses interactively.\n60\t# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase\n61\t# 4-bis re-run: no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED\n62\t# CONSEQUENCE: this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken before\n63\t# and after this commit are NOT comparable (S352 rule: re-test on a new\n64\t# generation, instrument intact). The 93/93/91 validity series measured in\n65\t# S352 was taken under 0.147.0.\n66\t\n67\t# PLAN-189 update (S356 2026-09-18, pack codex-pin-0155): widened upper bound\n68\t# to <0.156.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.155.0 is in-range. 0.155.0\n69\t# was published to npm on 2026-09-17; with the ADR-182 exact-version payload\n70\t# manifest the pair-rail went fail-CLOSED in this repo (`--verify-codex-pin`\n71\t# -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch) until this re-pin. LOWER BOUND\n72\t# UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape), executed\n73\t# OUTSIDE any open release window: GA v1.4.0 was cut 2026-09-15 and\n74\t# v1.4.1-rc.1 is cut only AFTER this commit. Per ADR-111\n75\t# §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase 4-bis re-run:\n76\t# no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n77\t# (same as S352): this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken\n78\t# before and after this commit are NOT comparable. The payload manifest\n79\t# (re-pinned in this same pack: payload sha256 b0b14f9c... for\n80\t# 0.155.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity recorded from the PLATFORM\n81\t# artifact per ADR-182 §5 step 2) remains the real supply-chain gate; this\n82\t# semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n83\t# Doctrine (S355): the Codex CLI is a SHA-pinned substrate — every Codex\n84\t# upgrade requires this re-pin BEFORE any release cut; never a casual\n85\t# `npm update -g`.\n86\t\n87\t# PLAN-193 update (S357 2026-09-23, pack codex-pin-0156): widened upper bound\n88\t# to <0.157.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.156.1 is in-range. 0.156.1\n89\t# was published to npm on 2026-09-23 as a hotfix of 0.156.0 (never pinned\n90\t# here). With the ADR-182 exact-version payload manifest, installing it before\n91\t# this re-pin closes the pair-rail (measured 2026-09-23 against the Owner's\n92\t# installed 0.156.1: `--verify-codex-pin` -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch),\n93\t# so the ceremony refuses to sign unless the installed payload already hashes\n94\t# to the sha256 pinned below. LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n95\t# (widen-upper-only; raising it past 0.139.0 would put the Codex host-adapter\n96\t# fixtures, recorded under codex-cli 0.139.0, out of range). Landed only AFTER\n97\t# the v1.4.1 GA tag (the ceremony refuses otherwise): release.yml step 15\n98\t# checks the GA verdict's codex_cli against this range and its\n99\t# codex_payload_sha256 against the manifest of the TAGGED tree, and this file\n100\t# is hashed into the verdict's inputs_hash. DECLARED EXCEPTION to the S355\n101\t# doctrine above: the Owner installed 0.156.1 globally on 2026-09-23, before\n102\t# the v1.4.1 GA cut, so for that one cut the letter of \"every Codex upgrade\n103\t# requires this re-pin BEFORE any release cut\" is not met. What still holds:\n104\t# the validator that step 15 runs accepts the GA verdict only if the\n105\t# verdict DECLARES a codex_cli inside the tagged range and the payload sha256\n106\t# of the tagged manifest (0.155.0) — a check of the declaration, not a hash of\n107\t# the binary that produced the verdict — so before these bytes land no verdict\n108\t# declaring 0.156.1 validates; step 15's optional mode\n109\t# (CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1, a repository variable unset on\n110\t# 2026-09-23) goes beyond tolerating a failed validation: it also skips a\n111\t# missing verdict file and drops the parent-SHA bind; the delta+ancestry\n112\t# gate that follows it fails closed in that mode. Landing\n113\t# these bytes before the tag would instead break the GA's own step 15\n114\t# (inputs_hash and payload pin both change under a verdict produced on\n115\t# 0.155.0). Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5 (the\n116\t# `§pin-update-protocol` label above names no heading in ADR-111) — a CLI\n117\t# bump reopens the corpus only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp. No\n118\t# locked-corpus run was taken for this bump (the runner's default corpus path\n119\t# is absent from this repository and its per-fixture review is still a stub),\n120\t# so the trigger is unevaluated, not passed. The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is\n121\t# deferred to the substrate wave, as declared in S356 (which recorded the S352\n122\t# re-pin as the same posture): it re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while\n123\t# what forces this re-pin is Codex as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n124\t# of that deferral: the installer's Codex-harness version-skew warning\n125\t# (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) reads this same range, so widening it admits\n126\t# 0.156.x as in-range for Codex as a hook host while the hook evidence stays\n127\t# at 0.139.0 — a re-certification this deferral knowingly waives (every\n128\t# widening since that reader landed, on 2026-07-10, had the same effect).\n129\t# From 0.155.0 to 0.156.0 the exec crate's output-shape change is confined to\n130\t# web-search items of the `codex exec --json` stream, which has no reader in\n131\t# live code (the live rail runs `exec -o` without `--json`, and the one parser\n132\t# of that stream in the tracked tree outside .claude/plans/ has no caller\n133\t# outside tests; the ADR-161 live-fire procedures under .claude/plans/PLAN-155/\n134\t# do read that stream, but items other than web search — the only kind the\n135\t# change touches — and stay deferred with the checklist); from 0.156.0 to\n136\t# 0.156.1 the exec crate is unchanged (same git tree at both tags)\n137\t# and, outside tests, only the workspace version, the bundled model catalog\n138\t# and two TUI source files change — upstream says that catalog also feeds the\n139\t# sub-agent tool descriptions sent to the model.\n140\t# DECLARED CONSEQUENCE (same as S352/S356): this changes the INSTRUMENT —\n141\t# rail measurements taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable.\n142\t# The payload manifest (re-pinned in this same pack: payload sha256\n143\t# 0196e89f... for 0.156.1/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity recorded from\n144\t# the PLATFORM artifact per ADR-182 §5 step 2) remains the real supply-chain\n145\t# gate; this range is a version gate (the release.yml step-15 validator reads\n146\t# it, among others), not a supply-chain gate.\n147\t\n148\t# re-pin update (2026-10-02, pack codex-pin-0160; generated by\n149\t# .claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py): package_version 0.156.1 -> 0.160.0.\n150\t# Upper bound widened <0.157.0 -> <0.161.0; LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at\n151\t# >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only). The payload manifest is re-pinned in this\n152\t# same pack: payload sha256 112fae7a... for 0.160.0/aarch64-apple-darwin,\n153\t# npm_integrity from the PLATFORM artifact\n154\t# @openai/codex@0.160.0-darwin-arm64 (ADR-182 §5 step 2).\n155\t# Why now: Owner decision of 2026-10-02 (S362), recorded in PLAN-194 as plan\n156\t# B (manual re-pin from the newest mold, ADR-182 §5): this re-pin is the\n157\t# FIRST task of the v1.4.3 maintenance train. PLAN-194 pending decision 3\n158\t# (how the automatic pin is packaged) was NOT taken, so the automatic Codex\n159\t# pin (PLAN-194 W3) moves after v1.4.3 and its Security VETO stays raised;\n160\t# until it lands, every Codex upgrade goes through a pack generated like\n161\t# this one.\n162\t# Release window: executed OUTSIDE any open release window. GA v1.4.2 was\n163\t# cut on 2026-09-30 and no v1.4.3 tag exists; the ceremony refuses to run\n164\t# unless the v1.4.2 tag is an ancestor of HEAD. Doctrine (S355) met: this\n165\t# re-pin lands BEFORE the next release cut. Only the UPPER bound widens; the\n166\t# lower bound stays where it was (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape).\n167\t# The payload manifest remains the real supply-chain gate; this range is a\n168\t# version gate.\n169\t# Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5, reopens the corpus\n170\t# only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp on the locked corpus. That\n171\t# trigger is NOT EVALUABLE in this tree: no locked-corpus run exists for\n172\t# this bump (the runner's default corpus path is absent from this repository\n173\t# and its per-fixture review is still a stub), so it is unevaluated, not\n174\t# passed.\n175\t# The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is DEFERRED, as in S352, S356 and S357: it\n176\t# re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while what forces this re-pin is Codex\n177\t# as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE of that deferral, stated by\n178\t# shape: every consumer that reads this range as a version gate admits\n179\t# 0.160.x from this commit on, the installer's Codex-harness version-skew\n180\t# check (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) among them, while the hook evidence it\n181\t# names stays certified on 0.139.0.\n182\t# DECLARED CONSEQUENCE (same as S352, S356 and S357): this changes the\n183\t# INSTRUMENT. The rail reviewer becomes the 0.160.0 binary; rail\n184\t# measurements taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable, and\n185\t# the first rail round on 0.160.0 is a re-test. What the reviewer serves is\n186\t# chosen by the Owner's Codex config, not by this pin: measured on\n187\t# 2026-10-02 (S362 probe of 0.160.0 in a disposable npm prefix) as model\n188\t# gpt-6-astra at reasoning effort xhigh. A change of that config changes the\n189\t# instrument without touching these bytes.\n190\t# Residual, by shape: the pin attests ONE executable, the\n191\t# aarch64-apple-darwin payload at the manifest path. Every other executable\n192\t# is outside the sha: the sibling executables the platform tarball carries\n193\t# beside it, the payloads of the other npm platforms, and the launcher of\n194\t# the main package (bin/codex.js). Same posture as every earlier generation,\n195\t# not a regression of this pack.\n196\t# Current compatibility floor (Onda6B): stable Codex CLI releases at or above\n197\t# 0.128.0 are compatible version evidence. This unbounded range is not a\n198\t# payload-hash attestation; codex-cli-pin-manifest.json remains that gate.\n199\t>=0.128.0\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57bd0a0f-ef05-4951-aa49-b19ce0916105","uuid":"0fbce7b8-0c60-4a83-afa0-7c54b1c4757b","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:37:48.395Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt","content":"# Codex CLI version pin — PLAN-081 Phase 6 / R1 C5 BLOCKING per TDE MF-6\n#\n# Format: semver range. release.yml step 15 + scripts/local/pair-rail-gate.sh\n# pre-flight assert that `codex --version` resolves to a version in this range.\n# Pin update ceremony: requires Phase 4-bis re-run + GPG sign + ADR amendment\n# IF catch_rate shifts >5pp on the locked corpus.\n#\n# Initial range chosen to cover the Phase 0A SPIKE-VERDICT.md baseline.\n#\n# v1.16.0 update (Phase 6-bis 2026-05-11 S101-cont): widened upper bound\n# to <0.131.0 so Owner's actual binary at codex-cli 0.130.0 is in-range.\n# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol, this widening does NOT trigger Phase\n# 4-bis re-run because no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken\n# yet (initial corpus run is itself part of v1.16.0 GA scope). If post-GA\n# the promotion-gate run shows catch_rate shift >5pp on 0.130.x vs\n# 0.128.x baseline, ADR-111 amendment + corpus re-run triggers.\n#\n# PLAN-142 update (S246 2026-06-19): widened upper bound to <0.140.0 so the\n# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.139.0 is in-range — the migration that restored\n# the pair-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin\n# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain\n# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per\n# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check\n# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.\n#\n# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to\n# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the\n# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are\n# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED\n# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an\n# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a\n# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release\n# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).\n# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md\n# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose\n# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`\n# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|\n# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;\n# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869\n# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner\n# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).\n#\n# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to\n# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump\n# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already\n# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release\n# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182\n# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json, re-pinned in this same pack:\n# payload sha256 19c4f144... for 0.147.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity\n# recorded from the platform artifact) remains the real supply-chain gate;\n# this semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n# Locked-corpus catch_rate check (ADR-111 §2): Owner elects run-vs-defer at\n# pack signing, recorded in the SENT-S318 sentinel Scope.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S352 2026-09-15): widened upper bound to <0.155.0 so the\n# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.154.0 is in-range. The rail was pinned at\n# 0.147.0 while the global CLI had moved SEVEN releases ahead, so every rail\n# round ran on a revisor older than the one the Owner uses interactively.\n# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase\n# 4-bis re-run: no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED\n# CONSEQUENCE: this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken before\n# and after this commit are NOT comparable (S352 rule: re-test on a new\n# generation, instrument intact). The 93/93/91 validity series measured in\n# S352 was taken under 0.147.0.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S356 2026-09-18, pack codex-pin-0155): widened upper bound\n# to <0.156.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.155.0 is in-range. 0.155.0\n# was published to npm on 2026-09-17; with the ADR-182 exact-version payload\n# manifest the pair-rail went fail-CLOSED in this repo (`--verify-codex-pin`\n# -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch) until this re-pin. LOWER BOUND\n# UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape), executed\n# OUTSIDE any open release window: GA v1.4.0 was cut 2026-09-15 and\n# v1.4.1-rc.1 is cut only AFTER this commit. Per ADR-111\n# §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase 4-bis re-run:\n# no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n# (same as S352): this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken\n# before and after this commit are NOT comparable. The payload manifest\n#