{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wvvLzv19XR5Ja9LD8uywJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t# ============================================================================\n3\t# _release_bump_sites.py — the ONE source of truth for the release version\n4\t# sites, and the only writer of them.\n5\t#\n6\t# Why a module and not a heredoc. Until PLAN-166/W0 this table lived inside\n7\t# `release.sh` as a `python3 - <<'PY'` heredoc. That had two costs that both\n8\t# showed up in the v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass:\n9\t#\n10\t#   1. the site list existed TWICE — once in the heredoc (the writer) and once\n11\t#      in the driver's `VERSION_FILES` array (the dry-run restore list). A list\n12\t#      that must match another list by hand does not stay matched; a restore\n13\t#      list shorter than the write list leaves debris (the S273 class).\n14\t#   2. it was untestable. `--today` could not be pinned, so the D+1\n15\t#      non-idempotence (F2) could not be exercised by a test.\n16\t#\n17\t# Both are closed here: the driver DERIVES its restore list from\n18\t# `print-sites --include-generated`, and `--today` is a REQUIRED parameter with\n19\t# NO DEFAULT (a parameter that changes the verdict never has a default —\n20\t# frozen-evidence lesson).\n21\t#\n22\t# Idempotence contract (F2). A `last-reviewed:` stamp asserts \"this document\n23\t# was re-read FOR THIS RELEASE\". Re-dating it without re-reading is a false\n24\t# claim on a surface that a signed tag then covers. So the stamp sites\n25\t# skip the ENTIRE line — neither date nor version — when the version already\n26\t# on the stamp is the target. `--restamp` is the named, explicit route for a\n27\t# real re-review.\n28\t#\n29\t# The two stamp oracles (do not collapse them). `npm/README.md` is watched by\n30\t# verify-counts' VERSION_SITES; SBOM.md / SECURITY.md / VERSIONING.md are\n31\t# watched ONLY by check-canonical-doc-freshness.py. Both oracles decide on the\n32\t# VERSION in the stamp, never on the date — which is what makes freezing the\n33\t# date safe.\n34\t#\n35\t# The support window (kinds \"minor\"/\"prev_minor\" — v1.3.0 re-pass, F-sites).\n36\t# verify-counts' VERSION_SITES also watches \"Current MINOR (vX.Y.x)\" and\n37\t# \"Previous MINOR (vX.Y.x)\" in SECURITY.md and VERSIONING.md (S293). Those\n38\t# sites were OUTSIDE this table at birth, so the next MINOR bump would write\n39\t# everything else, then DIE at the driver's own verify-counts call with a\n40\t# half-written tree (outside --dry-run there is no restore trap). The rule the\n41\t# oracle enforces is mechanical — Current = the target's minor, Previous = the\n42\t# minor immediately before it — so this writer derives both from --target and\n43\t# the \"ONE source of truth\" claim above stays true. The single non-derivable\n44\t# case, an X.0.0 target, is SKIPPED loudly and never guessed: the oracle\n45\t# cannot value-check it either (it derives prev=\"\" at X.0), and a MAJOR\n46\t# support-window transition is release-train judgment, not sed.\n47\t# ============================================================================\n48\t\"\"\"Release version-site table + writer (stdlib only, Python >= 3.9).\"\"\"\n49\t\n50\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n51\t\n52\timport argparse\n53\timport os\n54\timport re\n55\timport sys\n56\tfrom typing import Callable, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n57\t\n58\tSEMVER = r\"\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\"\n59\tSTAMP_RX = r\"(last-reviewed: )(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2})( +v)(\" + SEMVER + r\")\"\n60\tDATE_RX = re.compile(r\"\\A\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\Z\")\n61\t\n62\t# Kinds:\n63\t#   \"plain\"      — literal regex substitution, no stamp semantics.\n64\t#   \"stamp\"      — \"last-reviewed: <date> v<version>\"; skipped wholesale when\n65\t#                  the version already equals the target (unless --restamp).\n66\t#   \"minor\"      — support-window site carrying the TARGET's minor (vX.Y.x).\n67\t#   \"prev_minor\" — support-window site carrying the minor immediately BEFORE\n68\t#                  the target; not derivable at X.0.0 (skipped loudly there).\n69\tPLAIN = \"plain\"\n70\tSTAMP = \"stamp\"\n71\tMINOR = \"minor\"\n72\tPREV_MINOR = \"prev_minor\"\n73\t\n74\t# (path, kind, pattern) — patterns anchored exactly as their oracle checks\n75\t# them, so historical version mentions elsewhere in the file are never touched.\n76\t_SITES: List[Tuple[str, str, str]] = [\n77\t    (\"VERSION\", PLAIN, r\"\\A\\s*\" + SEMVER + r\"\\s*\\Z\"),\n78\t    # PLAN-169 W2.6 (ledger E.1/F.7/A.0.4): the install-state marker is the\n79\t    # surface check-framework-updates.sh reads MARKER-FIRST — a bump that\n80\t    # skips it leaves every adopter's updater reporting behind-minor\n81\t    # forever. Joins _SITES with its oracle mirror in verify-counts\n82\t    # VERSION_SITES (no census numeral here: the F6 guard forbids\n83\t    # site-count claims in comments, ordinals included).\n84\t    (\".claude/.framework-version\", PLAIN, r\"\\A\\s*\" + SEMVER + r\"\\s*\\Z\"),\n85\t    (\"npm/package.json\", PLAIN, r'(\"version\"\\s*:\\s*\")' + SEMVER + r'(\")'),\n86\t    (\"pyproject.toml\", PLAIN, r'(?m)^(version\\s*=\\s*\")' + SEMVER + r'(\")'),\n87\t    # The upgrade instructions resolve the latest RC tag during the hold and\n88\t    # use the GA tag afterwards. One pattern owns both version stems, so a\n89\t    # bump cannot leave either route on a prior train.\n90\t    (\"INSTALL.md\", PLAIN, r\"((?:--pin |git tag --list ['\\\"]?)v)\" + SEMVER),\n91\t    (\n92\t        \"docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\",\n93\t        PLAIN,\n94\t        r\"(currently\\s+v)\" + SEMVER + r\"(, aligned with the repo)\",\n95\t    ),\n96\t    # README.md and CLAUDE.md are deliberately NOT rows here: neither is a\n97\t    # version site. `VERSION=` never existed in either (verify-counts dropped\n98\t    # its dead rules for both in S291 — `git log -S 'VERSION='` finds no\n99\t    # commit that added one — and the release checklist states the same). A\n100\t    # writer row for a site no oracle watches would be that dead rule\n101\t    # reintroduced on the WRITE side: the day someone adds a `VERSION=` line\n102\t    # to README.md, the bump would rewrite a file every other surface\n103\t    # declares out of scope.\n104\t    (\"SBOM.md\", PLAIN, r\"(\\*\\*Version:\\*\\* `)\" + SEMVER + r\"(`)\"),\n105\t    # --- the support window (oracle: verify-counts VERSION_SITES modes\n106\t    #     \"minor\"/\"prev_minor\", S293). Patterns anchored exactly as the\n107\t    #     oracle's — SECURITY.md bolds the label, VERSIONING.md does not. ---\n108\t    (\"SECURITY.md\", MINOR, r\"(\\*\\*Current MINOR\\*\\* \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n109\t    (\"VERSIONING.md\", MINOR, r\"(Current MINOR \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n110\t    (\"SECURITY.md\", PREV_MINOR, r\"(\\*\\*Previous MINOR\\*\\* \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n111\t    (\"VERSIONING.md\", PREV_MINOR, r\"(Previous MINOR \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n112\t    # --- the review stamps (idempotence-critical; the table IS the census,\n113\t    #     a numeral here would be a mirror that drifts) ---\n114\t    (\"npm/README.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n115\t    (\"SBOM.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n116\t    (\"SECURITY.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n117\t    (\"VERSIONING.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n118\t]\n119\t\n120\t# Written by the bump PHASE but not by this module: `build-plugin.py\n121\t# --write-manifests` regenerates them from VERSION. They belong in any\n122\t# derived restore/guard list, which is why they are exported here instead of\n123\t# being re-typed by every caller (the duplicated-list failure this module\n124\t# exists to kill).\n125\tGENERATED_BY_BUMP: List[str] = [\n126\t    \".claude-plugin/plugin.json\",\n127\t    \".claude-plugin/marketplace.json\",\n128\t]\n129\t\n130\t\n131\tdef site_paths(include_generated: bool = False) -> List[str]:\n132\t    \"\"\"Every path this module may write, de-duplicated, in table order.\"\"\"\n133\t    out: List[str] = []\n134\t    for path, _kind, _rx in _SITES:\n135\t        if path not in out:\n136\t            out.append(path)\n137\t    if include_generated:\n138\t        for path in GENERATED_BY_BUMP:\n139\t            if path not in out:\n140\t                out.append(path)\n141\t    return out\n142\t\n143\t\n144\tdef _plain_replacement(pattern: str, target: str) -> str:\n145\t    \"\"\"Replacement string for a PLAIN site, rebuilt from its group count.\"\"\"\n146\t    if pattern.startswith(r\"\\A\"):  # the bare VERSION file\n147\t        return target + \"\\n\"\n148\t    groups = re.compile(pattern).groups\n149\t    if groups == 0:\n150\t        return target\n151\t    if groups == 1:\n152\t        return r\"\\g<1>\" + target\n153\t    return r\"\\g<1>\" + target + r\"\\g<2>\"\n154\t\n155\t\n156\tdef _stamp_replacer(\n157\t    target: str, today: str, restamp: bool\n158\t) -> Callable[[\"re.Match\"], str]:\n159\t    def _repl(m: \"re.Match\") -> str:\n160\t        if not restamp and m.group(4) == target:\n161\t            # Defense in depth: the whole line is left byte-identical. Both\n162\t            # stamp oracles read the VERSION, so freezing the date costs\n163\t            # nothing and re-dating without re-reading would be a false claim.\n164\t            return m.group(0)\n165\t        return m.group(1) + today + m.group(3) + target\n166\t\n167\t    return _repl\n168\t\n169\t\n170\tdef bump(\n171\t    target: str,\n172\t    today: str,\n173\t    *,\n174\t    restamp: bool = False,\n175\t    root: Optional[str] = None,\n176\t    out=None,\n177\t) -> int:\n178\t    \"\"\"Rewrite every version site to `target`. Returns files CHANGED.\"\"\"\n179\t    if not DATE_RX.match(today):\n180\t        raise ValueError(\"--today must be YYYY-MM-DD, got %r\" % (today,))\n181\t    if not re.match(r\"\\A\" + SEMVER + r\"\\Z\", target):\n182\t        raise ValueError(\"--target must be a bare semver, got %r\" % (target,))\n183\t    stream = out if out is not None else sys.stdout\n184\t    base = root or os.getcwd()\n185\t    # Support-window derivation, BEFORE any byte is written: whether every\n186\t    # site is writable is decided up front, never discovered mid-loop with a\n187\t    # half-bumped tree behind it.\n188\t    _maj, _min = (int(x) for x in target.split(\".\")[:2])\n189\t    minor_target = \"%d.%d\" % (_maj, _min)\n190\t    prev_minor = \"%d.%d\" % (_maj, _min - 1) if _min > 0 else None\n191\t    changed = 0\n192\t    for path, kind, pattern in _SITES:\n193\t        if kind == PREV_MINOR and prev_minor is None:\n194\t            # X.0.0: Previous MINOR is not derivable from the target, and the\n195\t            # oracle skips value-checking it there too (prev=\"\" at X.0). Never\n196\t            # guess a support-window promise — leave it and say so, loudly.\n197\t            print(\n198\t                \"  !!   %s: Previous MINOR left untouched — not derivable \"\n199\t                \"from %s (X.0.0); the support window needs release-train \"\n200\t                \"judgment here\" % (path, target),"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57bd0a0f-ef05-4951-aa49-b19ce0916105","uuid":"8b65eff4-7308-4092-a932-2d9820db82d0","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:39:28.595Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/scripts/local/_release_bump_sites.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# ============================================================================\n# _release_bump_sites.py — the ONE source of truth for the release version\n# sites, and the only writer of them.\n#\n# Why a module and not a heredoc. Until PLAN-166/W0 this table lived inside\n# `release.sh` as a `python3 - <<'PY'` heredoc. That had two costs that both\n# showed up in the v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass:\n#\n#   1. the site list existed TWICE — once in the heredoc (the writer) and once\n#      in the driver's `VERSION_FILES` array (the dry-run restore list). A list\n#      that must match another list by hand does not stay matched; a restore\n#      list shorter than the write list leaves debris (the S273 class).\n#   2. it was untestable. `--today` could not be pinned, so the D+1\n#      non-idempotence (F2) could not be exercised by a test.\n#\n# Both are closed here: the driver DERIVES its restore list from\n# `print-sites --include-generated`, and `--today` is a REQUIRED parameter with\n# NO DEFAULT (a parameter that changes the verdict never has a default —\n# frozen-evidence lesson).\n#\n# Idempotence contract (F2). A `last-reviewed:` stamp asserts \"this document\n# was re-read FOR THIS RELEASE\". Re-dating it without re-reading is a false\n# claim on a surface that a signed tag then covers. So the stamp sites\n# skip the ENTIRE line — neither date nor version — when the version already\n# on the stamp is the target. `--restamp` is the named, explicit route for a\n# real re-review.\n#\n# The two stamp oracles (do not collapse them). `npm/README.md` is watched by\n# verify-counts' VERSION_SITES; SBOM.md / SECURITY.md / VERSIONING.md are\n# watched ONLY by check-canonical-doc-freshness.py. Both oracles decide on the\n# VERSION in the stamp, never on the date — which is what makes freezing the\n# date safe.\n#\n# The support window (kinds \"minor\"/\"prev_minor\" — v1.3.0 re-pass, F-sites).\n# verify-counts' VERSION_SITES also watches \"Current MINOR (vX.Y.x)\" and\n# \"Previous MINOR (vX.Y.x)\" in SECURITY.md and VERSIONING.md (S293). Those\n# sites were OUTSIDE this table at birth, so the next MINOR bump would write\n# everything else, then DIE at the driver's own verify-counts call with a\n# half-written tree (outside --dry-run there is no restore trap). The rule the\n# oracle enforces is mechanical — Current = the target's minor, Previous = the\n# minor immediately before it — so this writer derives both from --target and\n# the \"ONE source of truth\" claim above stays true. The single non-derivable\n# case, an X.0.0 target, is SKIPPED loudly and never guessed: the oracle\n# cannot value-check it either (it derives prev=\"\" at X.0), and a MAJOR\n# support-window transition is release-train judgment, not sed.\n# ============================================================================\n\"\"\"Release version-site table + writer (stdlib only, Python >= 3.9).\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Callable, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n\nSEMVER = r\"\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\"\nSTAMP_RX = r\"(last-reviewed: )(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2})( +v)(\" + SEMVER + r\")\"\nDATE_RX = re.compile(r\"\\A\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\Z\")\n\n# Kinds:\n#   \"plain\"      — literal regex substitution, no stamp semantics.\n#   \"stamp\"      — \"last-reviewed: <date> v<version>\"; skipped wholesale when\n#                  the version already equals the target (unless --restamp).\n#   \"minor\"      — support-window site carrying the TARGET's minor (vX.Y.x).\n#   \"prev_minor\" — support-window site carrying the minor immediately BEFORE\n#                  the target; not derivable at X.0.0 (skipped loudly there).\nPLAIN = \"plain\"\nSTAMP = \"stamp\"\nMINOR = \"minor\"\nPREV_MINOR = \"prev_minor\"\n\n# (path, kind, pattern) — patterns anchored exactly as their oracle checks\n# them, so historical version mentions elsewhere in the file are never touched.\n_SITES: List[Tuple[str, str, str]] = [\n    (\"VERSION\", PLAIN, r\"\\A\\s*\" + SEMVER + r\"\\s*\\Z\"),\n    # PLAN-169 W2.6 (ledger E.1/F.7/A.0.4): the install-state marker is the\n    # surface check-framework-updates.sh reads MARKER-FIRST — a bump that\n    # skips it leaves every adopter's updater reporting behind-minor\n    # forever. Joins _SITES with its oracle mirror in verify-counts\n    # VERSION_SITES (no census numeral here: the F6 guard forbids\n    # site-count claims in comments, ordinals included).\n    (\".claude/.framework-version\", PLAIN, r\"\\A\\s*\" + SEMVER + r\"\\s*\\Z\"),\n    (\"npm/package.json\", PLAIN, r'(\"version\"\\s*:\\s*\")' + SEMVER + r'(\")'),\n    (\"pyproject.toml\", PLAIN, r'(?m)^(version\\s*=\\s*\")' + SEMVER + r'(\")'),\n    # The upgrade instructions resolve the latest RC tag during the hold and\n    # use the GA tag afterwards. One pattern owns both version stems, so a\n    # bump cannot leave either route on a prior train.\n    (\"INSTALL.md\", PLAIN, r\"((?:--pin |git tag --list ['\\\"]?)v)\" + SEMVER),\n    (\n        \"docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\",\n        PLAIN,\n        r\"(currently\\s+v)\" + SEMVER + r\"(, aligned with the repo)\",\n    ),\n    # README.md and CLAUDE.md are deliberately NOT rows here: neither is a\n    # version site. `VERSION=` never existed in either (verify-counts dropped\n    # its dead rules for both in S291 — `git log -S 'VERSION='` finds no\n    # commit that added one — and the release checklist states the same). A\n    # writer row for a site no oracle watches would be that dead rule\n    # reintroduced on the WRITE side: the day someone adds a `VERSION=` line\n    # to README.md, the bump would rewrite a file every other surface\n    # declares out of scope.\n    (\"SBOM.md\", PLAIN, r\"(\\*\\*Version:\\*\\* `)\" + SEMVER + r\"(`)\"),\n    # --- the support window (oracle: verify-counts VERSION_SITES modes\n    #     \"minor\"/\"prev_minor\", S293). Patterns anchored exactly as the\n    #     oracle's — SECURITY.md bolds the label, VERSIONING.md does not. ---\n    (\"SECURITY.md\", MINOR, r\"(\\*\\*Current MINOR\\*\\* \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n    (\"VERSIONING.md\", MINOR, r\"(Current MINOR \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n    (\"SECURITY.md\", PREV_MINOR, r\"(\\*\\*Previous MINOR\\*\\* \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n    (\"VERSIONING.md\", PREV_MINOR, r\"(Previous MINOR \\(`v)\\d+\\.\\d+(\\.x`\\))\"),\n    # --- the review stamps (idempotence-critical; the table IS the census,\n    #     a numeral here would be a mirror that drifts) ---\n    (\"npm/README.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n    (\"SBOM.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n    (\"SECURITY.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n    (\"VERSIONING.md\", STAMP, STAMP_RX),\n]\n\n# Written by the bump PHASE but not by this module: `build-plugin.py\n# --write-manifests` regenerates them from VERSION. They belong in any\n# derived restore/guard list, which is why they are exported here instead of\n# being re-typed by every caller (the duplicated-list failure this module\n# exists to kill).\nGENERATED_BY_BUMP: List[str] = [\n    \".claude-plugin/plugin.json\",\n    \".claude-plugin/marketplace.json\",\n]\n\n\ndef site_paths(include_generated: bool = False) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Every path this module may write, de-duplicated, in table order.\"\"\"\n    out: List[str] = []\n    for path, _kind, _rx in _SITES:\n        if path not in out:\n            out.append(path)\n    if include_generated:\n        for path in GENERATED_BY_BUMP:\n            if path not in out:\n                out.append(path)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _plain_replacement(pattern: str, target: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Replacement string for a PLAIN site, rebuilt from its group count.\"\"\"\n    if pattern.startswith(r\"\\A\"):  # the bare VERSION file\n        return target + \"\\n\"\n    groups = re.compile(pattern).groups\n    if groups == 0:\n        return target\n    if groups == 1:\n        return r\"\\g<1>\" + target\n    return r\"\\g<1>\" + target + r\"\\g<2>\"\n\n\ndef _stamp_replacer(\n    target: str, today: str, restamp: bool\n) -> Callable[[\"re.Match\"], str]:\n    def _repl(m: \"re.Match\") -> str:\n        if not restamp and m.group(4) == target:\n            # Defense in depth: the whole line is left byte-identical. Both\n            # stamp oracles read the VERSION, so freezing the date costs\n            # nothing and re-dating without re-reading would be a false claim.\n            return m.group(0)\n        return m.group(1) + today + m.group(3) + target\n\n    return _repl\n\n\ndef bump(\n    target: str,\n    today: str,\n    *,\n    restamp: bool = False,\n    root: Optional[str] = None,\n    out=None,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rewrite every version site to `target`. Returns files CHANGED.\"\"\"\n    if not DATE_RX.match(today):\n        raise ValueError(\"--today must be YYYY-MM-DD, got %r\" % (today,))\n    if not re.match(r\"\\A\" + SEMVER + r\"\\Z\", target):\n        raise ValueError(\"--target must be a bare semver, got %r\" % (target,))\n    stream = out if out is not None else sys.stdout\n    base = root or os.getcwd()\n    # Support-window derivation, BEFORE any byte is written: whether every\n    # site is writable is decided up front, never discovered mid-loop with a\n    # half-bumped tree behind it.\n    _maj, _min = (int(x) for x in target.split(\".\")[:2])\n    minor_target = \"%d.%d\" % (_maj, _min)\n    prev_minor = \"%d.%d\" % (_maj, _min - 1) if _min > 0 else None\n    changed = 0\n    for path, kind, pattern in _SITES:\n        if kind == PREV_MINOR and prev_minor is None:\n            # X.0.0: Previous MINOR is not derivable from the target, and the\n            # oracle skips value-checking it there too (prev=\"\" at X.0). Never\n            # guess a support-window promise — leave it and say so, loudly.\n            print(\n                \"  !!   %s: Previous MINOR left untouched — not derivable \"\n                \"from %s (X.0.0); the support window needs release-train \"\n                \"judgment here\" % (path, target),","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":303}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016wvvLzv19XR5Ja9LD8uywJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
