{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V6B7amyFQ4WzKEj3nEgjSo","type":"tool_result","content":"15:- Any change to a file under `SPEC/v1/` (additive or breaking)\n16:- Any change that introduces a **new trust boundary** an adopter must\n17:  accept (e.g. ADR-051 added the SHA-pinned skill-by-reference path → MINOR bump)\n28:- New optional CLI tools (`ceo-cost`, `ceo-health`, etc.) — additive,\n33:Format: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-rc.N]`.\n45:### MINOR — additive SPEC change OR new trust boundary\n49:- A new field is added to an existing event (always additive — see\n52:- A new trust boundary is introduced that adopters must understand\n62:| `v1.1.0 → v1.2.0` | PLAN-160/161/163/164 — Claude 5 model registry (ADR-181, additive `model:` contract), Codex payload-pin enforcement (ADR-182), pair-rail timeout contract (ADR-110-AMEND-1), new typed audit actions. |\n63:| `v1.2.0 → v1.3.0` | PLAN-162/165 — night-mode posture toggle (new trust boundary, ADR-185); sentinel-unlock provenance inside git worktrees (ADR-119 Invariant 5 — closes in-window self-authored-sentinel escalation); fail-CLOSED matcher deadline (ADR-186); pair-rail 180/210 + `timeout_ms` (ADR-110-AMEND-2). |\n65:### PATCH — bug fixes, additive features within SPEC\n81:Every MAJOR or MINOR bump goes through a **mandatory RC-to-GA hold**\n88:1. Cut `vMAJOR.MINOR.0-rc.1` tag on `main` HEAD.\n93:   the GA tag (`vMAJOR.MINOR.0`). `release.yml` rejects a GA tag cut\n177:6. The bump is a MINOR version (additive contract for adopters who\n189:| Current MINOR (`v1.4.x`) | Full support — features + security + bug fixes |\n190:| Previous MINOR (`v1.3.x`) | Security-only patches for **6 months** after the next MINOR ships |\n194:CHANGELOG.md for the sequence). Skipping a MINOR is supported across\n195:the v1 series but discouraged because each MINOR adds tests and\n198:## Backward compatibility within a MINOR\n214:| MINOR releases | ~ every 2–3 weeks so far (`v1.0.0` 07-01 → `v1.1.0` 07-13 →